  "ai_language_tip": "Use polite Burmese (my) with the polite particle (khin-bya/shin); English works at international hotels, larger private hospitals and some upscale Yangon businesses; ethnic-language areas still understand Burmese for business.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Fine at international hotels, big private hospitals and some Yangon offices; rare at local shops, clinics and outside Yangon/Mandalay.",
  "politeness": "Gentle and respectful: 'Mingalaba', address men as 'U'/'Ko' and women as 'Daw'/'Ma' by age, say you call on behalf of someone; end with 'kyay-zu-tin-ba-deh'. Avoid political topics entirely.",
  "name_tip": "Burmese names have no family surname; bookings go under the full given name, often with an honorific (Ko, Ma, U, Daw) — give the full name and spell if needed.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile numbers start 09 (e.g. 09 1234 5678; +95 drops the 0) with lengths varying by operator; Viber on the same number is the default follow-up channel; landlines are rarely used by small businesses.",
  "time_tip": "12-hour clock with day-part words (မနက် morning, နေ့လည် midday, ညနေ evening, ည night); 'ခွဲ' after the hour = :30 — always read back with the day part.",
  "number_tip": "Burmese digits (၀–၉) appear alongside Western digits; numbers are read digit by digit or in small groups; prices in kyat.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch (about 12:00–13:00), calls after 21:00, the Thingyan water festival in April (about a week of closures), and Buddhist full-moon holidays when some businesses close; power cuts can make lines unreachable.",
  "closed_days": "Saturday–Sunday for government and banks; shops and restaurants mostly open daily; Thingyan (mid-April, about 5–9 days of public holidays) and full-moon days (e.g. Thadingyut, Tazaungdaing) bring closures.",
  "booking_channels": "Phone and Viber dominate for clinics, salons and restaurants; Facebook pages and Messenger for shops and food; delivery apps (foodpanda, GrabFood) with changing coverage; payments by KBZPay, WavePay, AYA Pay or cash.",
  "voice_menu": "Telecoms and banks use Burmese/English IVR; hospitals have booking lines answered by staff; small businesses answer in person.",
  "callback_habits": "Businesses confirm or call back on Viber or by phone; clinics may call the day before; delivery riders call on arrival.",
